1
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:05,820
(Howard:)Ma, Ma, calm down.

2
00:00:06,010 --> 00:00:06,780
(Howard:)Listen to me.

3
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:08,610
(Howard:)I know it says click
with the mouse,

4
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:11,280
(Howard:)but on a laptop,
the trackpad is the mouse.

5
00:00:11,290 --> 00:00:13,820
(Howard:)Now, put your finger on it.

6
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:16,460
(Howard:)Doesn't matter which finger.

7
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:18,490
(Howard:)Good choice.

8
00:00:18,490 --> 00:00:22,400
(Howard:)Now move it down
to your e-mail icon.

9
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,260
(Howard:)Yeah, the little envelope.

10
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:26,700
(Howard:)What do you mean,
"What does it look like?"

11
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:28,770
(Howard:)It looks like an envelope!

12
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:30,440
(Howard:)Fine, you don't like
the computer,

13
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:32,240
(Howard:)don't use it!

14
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:35,780
(Howard:)Sure, we can exchange it
for a salad spinner. Good-bye!

15
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:42,110
(Raj:)That's a Hanukkah present
you're regretting, huh?

16
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:44,680
(Sheldon:)I won't say that
all senior citizens

17
00:00:44,690 --> 00:00:48,350
(Sheldon:)who can't master technology
should be publicly flogged,

18
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:50,860
(Sheldon:)but if we made an
example of one or two,

19
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:53,290
(Sheldon:)it might give the others
incentive to try harder.

20
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,330
(Leonard:)I had a great idea.

21
00:00:56,330 --> 00:00:57,800
(Leonard:)You know how
we're always having

22
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,700
(Leonard:)to stop and solve
differential equations,

23
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:01,550
(Leonard:)like when you're doing
Fourier analysis,

